                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "ReallyGoodBattle is a fighting game with a lot of heart and attention to detail put into it.\n\nI can tell that the developer has truly studied what has made fighting games in the past satisfying to play: There is plenty of rewarding feedback when confirming a kill, movement is fluid, fighting is balanced, jumping is responsive, and plenty of nuetral-game mechanics exist. All that combined allows all sorts of players to pick up and start fighting, regardless of their play style.\n\nWith all indie games, there are some pros and cons...\n\nPro:\n+ Unique fighting style and gameplay\n+ Attention to detail for deeper-level play\n+ Fast-paced\n+ Menu set-up allows players to easily get into new matches\n+ FUN!\n+ Local multiplayer!\n\nCon:\n- Gravity takes a bit to get used to\n- No single-player co-op at the moment\n\nI can easily see this game getting a huge following at Smash or other fighting game tournaments... Its addictive gameplay and depth makes me want to keep playing. If you're into fighting games, like I am, you'll have a lot of fun with this one!",
